# Keep eval reports and results (for CI)
!benchmark/datasets/*/eval/
!benchmark/datasets/*/results/
!benchmark/datasets/*/README.md

# HTML sketches and design artifacts
EMPTY-STATE-SKETCHES*.html

# Agent state directories (added 2026-09-06, epistemic audit N16)
.mimosa/

# Python bytecode (added 2026-09-06 — a tracked .pyc was previously committed)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Intentionally tracked exceptions to the rules above (classified 2026-09-14
# during the pre-commit artifact classification for the C1 evidence commit):
# - /Web-Prototype.zip is the web-audit design source-of-truth artifact and
#   stays tracked even though it matches the ignore pattern below.
# - outputs/agent-task-registry.md, outputs/delightful-experience-redesign-report.md,
#   and outputs/overview.md predate the outputs/ rule and stay tracked as
#   historical reports. NEW files under outputs/ remain ignored.
# Do not "fix" this drift with git rm --cached; untracking would delete the
# design source-of-truth and historical reports from the repo surface.
/Web-Prototype.zip

# TypeSafe Jev exploration artifacts (NM-R15 / EXP-JEV register, added 2026-09-19).
# Raw API captures and local replay state are tool outputs and stay local;
# calibration reports land under docs/research/ and stay tracked.
# The API key itself lives in .env (covered by the .env.* rule above) — never
# in tracked files.
tools/jev-replay/raw/
tools/jev-replay/cache/

# Perf-capture scratch outputs (perf-s14 tooling, added 2026-09-22 with the
# vision-council work). Evidence summaries land under benchmark/results/ and
# stay tracked; raw capture scratch stays local.
tools/perf-s14-capture/out/
*.xcresult
